# Pie Chart and Donut Chart

## Objective

To visualize the proportion of orders by device type using Pie and Donut charts.

## Dataset

Sales-Export_2019-2020.csv

## Device Types

- PC
- Mobile
- Tablet

## Visualizations

### Pie Chart

The Pie Chart shows the percentage share of orders made using each device type.

### Donut Chart

The Donut Chart is a modified Pie Chart with a hole in the centre. The total number of orders is displayed in the centre.

## Key Findings

- PC accounts for 78.5% of all orders.
- Mobile accounts for 14.2% of all orders.
- Tablet accounts for 7.3% of all orders.
- PC is the most commonly used device in this dataset.

## Important Data Analyst Insight

The device with the highest number of orders is not automatically the most profitable device.

To determine which device performs best financially, we should compare:

- Total Revenue
- Average Order Value
- Total Profit
- Profit Margin

## When to Use a Pie Chart

Use a Pie Chart when:

- Data represents parts of a whole.
- Categories are limited.
- Percentage/share is important.
- The total represents 100%.

## When Not to Use a Pie Chart

Avoid Pie Charts when:

- There are too many categories.
- Precise comparison is required.
- Data represents a time trend.
- Numerical distributions need to be analysed.

For many categories, a Bar Chart is usually easier to interpret.
